## Course overview

Physics at Standard Level develops a quantitative understanding of the physical world, from the motion of everyday objects to the behaviour of fields and quantum particles. The course is built around the IB's organising themes — **space, time and motion; the particulate nature of matter; wave behaviour; fields; and nuclear and quantum physics** — and emphasises modelling, measurement, and uncertainty.

## What you will study

- **Mechanics** — kinematics, forces, momentum, work, energy, and power.
- **Thermal physics** — temperature, internal energy, the gas laws, and the kinetic model.
- **Waves** — oscillations, wave behaviour, sound, and the electromagnetic spectrum.
- **Electricity & magnetism** — fields, current, circuits, and electromagnetic induction.
- **Modern physics** — atomic, nuclear, and an introduction to quantum effects.

## Assessment

| Component | Weighting | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 | 36% | Multiple choice + data analysis |
| Paper 2 | 44% | Short and extended response |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | Individual scientific investigation |

## The Internal Assessment

You design and carry out one experiment of your own, controlling variables, quantifying uncertainty, and evaluating your method. Strong investigations start from a question you actually want answered — a sport, an instrument, a phenomenon you noticed — not from a textbook recipe.
